[0.006, "o", "\u001b]11;?\u001b\\\u001b[6n"]
[20.522, "o", "1. **Router-sled end-grain cutting board:** glue up strips cut on the table saw with the four 36″ bar clamps, then flatten it with the Woodhaven sled, the 3-1/2 HP router and the 1-1/2″ surfacing bit.\r\n2. **French-cleat tool wall:** rip 45° cleats on the table saw and hang holders for the M18 tools, bike tools and clamps, which frees up pegboard and bench space.\r\n3. **Doweled wall rack for the household bikes:** cut it with the circular saw and speed square, drill the dowel holes on the drill press, and put a shelf on top for pumps and the bike tools.\r\n\r\nThe inventory lists the miter saw as gone, so plan to make crosscuts with the circular saw or the pull saw. The surfacing bit hasn't been confirmed as being in the shop, so check that it's there before you plan on idea 1.\r\n"]
